WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.082
Descriptive statistics summarize the main characteristics of the data you currently have.

00:00:06.082 --> 00:00:09.947
The mean describes the arithmetic average.

00:00:09.947 --> 00:00:13.317
The median describes the middle value.

00:00:13.317 --> 00:00:18.852
Standard deviation describes how spread out values are around the mean.

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:22.907
Quartiles describe positions within the ordered data.

00:00:22.907 --> 00:00:26.592
Run the code and inspect the describe output for order amount.

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:30.677
Notice that no single statistic tells the whole story.

00:00:30.677 --> 00:00:35.862
Two datasets can have the same mean but very different variability.

00:00:35.862 --> 00:00:42.367
A mean can also be affected by extreme values, while the median is usually more resistant.

00:00:42.367 --> 00:00:46.987
A good descriptive summary therefore uses several measures together.

00:00:46.987 --> 00:00:52.427
When you report statistics, always connect the number to the variable and units.

00:00:52.427 --> 00:00:58.650
Saying the mean is ninety is less informative than saying the mean order amount is ninety dollars.
